<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy, Terms & Conditions | Ariane Mader"
  seoTitle="Privacy Policy & Terms and Conditions | Ariane Mader"
  description="Read the privacy policy and terms and conditions for coaching, counselling, workshops, payments, cancellations, confidentiality, and data protection."
  canonicalUrl="https://www.arianemader.com/privacy-terms-conditions"
  lang="en"
  alternateEn="https://www.arianemader.com/privacy-terms-conditions"
  alternateDe="https://www.arianemader.com/de/privacy-terms-conditions"
  xDefault="https://www.arianemader.com/privacy-terms-conditions"
>
  <PageHeaderNoPicture 
    title="Privacy, Terms &amp; Conditions" 
    subtitle="Ariane Mader – Coaching &amp; Counselling"
  />
  
  
  <!-- About Me/Ariane -->
<section class="py-16 bg-white">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto prose prose-lg prose-max-w-none prose-p:my-2">

      <h2 class="blueFont">1. Introduction</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms &amp; Conditions apply to coaching and counselling services provided by <strong>Ariane Mader</strong> (the “Coach”).
        Individual arrangements, including session format and fees, may additionally be agreed in writing.
        The Privacy Policy below explains separately how personal data is processed.
      </p>

    <!-- Terms & Conditions Section Header -->
      <div class="my-12 text-center">
        <div class="border-t border-gray-300 mb-1"></div>

          <h2 class="text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wide text-base font-semibold">
            Terms & Conditions
          </h2>

        <div class="border-t border-gray-300 mt-6"></div>
      </div>

      <h2 class="blueFont">2. Professional Framework</h2>

      <h3>2.1 Role and Standards</h3>
      <p>
        The Coach operates as a sole proprietorship registered in the Netherlands and is a registered
        member of the <strong><a href="https://www.lvsc.eu/"><u>LVSC (Landelijke Vereniging voor Supervisie en Coaching)</u></a></strong> in the Netherlands,
        working in accordance with its professional <a href="https://www.lvsc.eu/sites/default/files/2024-09/lvsc-gedragscode-2016-english-version.pdf"><u>Code of Conduct</u></a>.
      </p>

      <h3>2.2 Nature of Coaching and Counselling</h3>
      <p>
        Coaching and counselling are reflective and developmental processes. They are
        <strong>not a substitute for psychotherapy, medical treatment, or crisis intervention</strong>,
        and are not intended to diagnose, treat, or cure mental health or medical conditions.
      </p>

      <h3>2.3 Scope of Services</h3>
      <p>
        Services may include, but are not limited to, individual coaching, counselling, workshops, masterclasses, and talks.
        Individual coaching and counselling sessions are primarily offered <strong>online</strong>. Other formats may be agreed separately.
      </p>

      <h3>2.4 Client Responsibility</h3>
      <p>
        Participation is voluntary and the Client remains responsible for their own decisions and actions. The Client remains
        responsible for their own active participation and progress between sessions, as well as their own physical and psychological boundaries. If support outside the
        scope of coaching appears necessary, the Coach may suggest referral to another qualified
        professional.
      </p>

      <h2 class="blueFont">3. Booking, Sessions, and Fees</h2>

      <h3>3.1 Booking and Format</h3>
      <ul class="green-bullets space-y-1 [&>li]:my-0">
        <li>Sessions must be booked in advance through contacting the Coach. Only once both sides have confirmed the booking, whether orally or in writing, is the session reserved.</li>
        <li>Before the first paid session, new Clients complete the relevant agreement, consent, and intake documents.</li>
        <li>Session duration is typically <strong>60 minutes</strong>, unless otherwise agreed.</li>
        <li>Sessions will end at their scheduled time regardless of the Client's arrival time.</li>
        <li>Periodic evaluations may take place to review goals and progress.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>3.2 Fees and Payment</h3>
      <ul class="green-bullets space-y-1 [&>li]:my-0">
        <li>Fees are listed on the website or agreed on during the initial contact or confirmed in writing.</li>
        <li>Invoices will be issued within one month after the session and are payable within <strong>14 days</strong> of the invoice date, unless otherwise agreed.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>3.3 Online Sessions</h3>
      <p>
        Both parties are responsible for ensuring a stable connection. In case of significant technical issues, the Coach will make reasonable efforts to find a suitable solution or reschedule.
      </p>

      <h2 class="blueFont">4. Cancellation and Termination</h2>
      <ul class="green-bullets space-y-1 [&>li]:my-0">
        <li>Cancellations must be made at least <strong>24 hours</strong> before the scheduled session.</li>
        <li>Late cancellations or no-shows may be charged at the full session rate.</li>
        <li>Exceptions may be made in emergencies at the Coach’s discretion.</li>
        <li>Either party may end the coaching or counselling relationship at any time. Any already confirmed session remains subject to the cancellation policy above.</li>
        <li>The Coach may end or decline services if continuation would be unethical, unsafe, or outside the professional scope.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="blueFont">5. Confidentiality</h2>
      <p>
        Information shared in coaching or counselling is treated confidentially. Information is disclosed only with the Client’s permission or where disclosure is required or otherwise permitted by law. In an acute safety situation, the Coach may take appropriate steps where legally justified.
      </p>
      <p>
        Session content may be discussed for professional reflection in intervision or supervision only where the Client has separately consented. Direct identifiers are not shared, and information is anonymised or abstracted as far as reasonably possible.
      </p>

      <h2 class="blueFont">6. Complaints</h2>
      <p>
        If the Client has a complaint, they are encouraged to discuss it directly with the Coach first.
      </p>
      <p>
        If the issue cannot be resolved, a complaint may be submitted in accordance with the
        <strong><a href="https://www.lvsc.eu/klachtenprocedure"><u>LVSC complaints procedure</u></a></strong>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="blueFont">7. Liability</h2>
      <p>
        Coaching and counselling are open-ended processes and no particular result or outcome is guaranteed. The Client remains responsible for their own decisions and actions.
        The Coach’s liability is governed by applicable law. To the extent permitted by law, liability for indirect or consequential loss is excluded. Nothing in these Terms excludes or limits liability where such exclusion or limitation is not permitted by law.
      </p>

      <h2 class="blueFont">8. Force Majeure</h2>
      <p>
        The Coach is not liable for failure or delay in fulfilling obligations due to circumstances beyond reasonable control (force majeure), including but not limited to illness, technical failures, or government restrictions.
        In such cases, sessions will be rescheduled where possible.
      </p>

      <h2 class="blueFont">9. Applicable Law</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms and any agreement between the Client and the Coach are governed by Dutch law. 
        Mandatory consumer rights that apply under applicable law remain unaffected.
      </p>
      
      <!-- Privacy Policy Section Header -->
      <div class="my-12 text-center">
        <div class="border-t border-gray-300 mb-1"></div>

          <h2 class="text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wide text-base font-semibold">
            Privacy Policy
          </h2>

        <div class="border-t border-gray-300 mt-6"></div>
      </div>

        <h2 class="blueFont">10. Privacy and Data Protection</h2>

        <h3>10.1 Data Controller</h3>
        <p>
          Ariane Mader is the controller responsible for the processing of personal data.<br>
          Email: <a href="mailto:info@arianemader.com" class="text-gray-800 hover:text-gray-600 transition-colors">info<span aria-hidden="true">[at]</span><span class="sr-only">@</span>arianemader.com</a><br>
          Postal address: <strong>Keurenplein 41 Box C4004, 1069CD Amsterdam</strong>, The Netherlands<br>
          Chamber of Commerce (KvK): <strong>98252305</strong><br>
          VAT ID: <strong>NL005320329B95</strong>
        </p>

        <h3>10.2 Personal Data and Purposes</h3>
        <p>Depending on the service and the information provided, personal data may include:</p>
        <ul class="green-bullets space-y-1 [&>li]:my-0">
          <li>name, pronouns, age, country, email address, and telephone number;</li>
          <li>billing address and other information required for invoicing;</li>
          <li>information provided in intake forms, emails, coaching or counselling sessions, and session notes;</li>
          <li>information about personal circumstances, goals, work, relationships, and wellbeing;</li>
          <li>health information voluntarily provided where relevant to the coaching or counselling process;</li>
          <li>appointment, agreement, payment, and other administrative information.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          These data are processed to communicate with Clients, arrange and provide services, tailor the coaching or counselling process, keep appropriate professional records, issue invoices and maintain accounting records, administer agreements and payments, and comply with legal obligations.
        </p>

        <h3>10.3 Legal Bases and Health Data</h3>
        <p>
          Personal data are processed where necessary to take steps at the Client’s request before entering into an agreement, to perform an agreement, to comply with legal obligations, or on the basis of consent where consent is the appropriate legal basis.
        </p>
        <p>
          Health data are special-category personal data. Where health information is voluntarily provided and its processing relies on consent, explicit consent is requested separately. Consent may be withdrawn at any time with effect for the future.
        </p>

        <h3>10.4 Service Providers and Data Sharing</h3>
        <p>
          Personal data may be processed using service providers that support the practice, including <strong>Zoho Mail</strong> for email, <strong>Microsoft OneDrive</strong> for file storage, and <strong>Google Calendar and Google Meet</strong> for scheduling and online sessions. The website is hosted through <strong>GitHub Pages</strong> and uses <strong>Cloudflare</strong> services as described below. These providers may process technical or personal data in accordance with their respective roles, terms, and privacy safeguards.
        </p>
        <p>
          Information is not sold. It is disclosed to other parties only where necessary for the services described above, where the Client has consented, or where there is another lawful basis or legal obligation.
        </p>

        <h3>10.5 Intervision and Supervision</h3>
        <p>
          Where the Client has separately consented, relevant session content may be discussed with professionally bound coaches or supervisors for intervision or supervision. Direct identifiers are not shared and information is anonymised or abstracted as far as reasonably possible.
        </p>

        <h3>10.6 Retention</h3>
        <ul class="green-bullets space-y-1 [&>li]:my-0">
          <li>Intake information and substantive coaching or counselling notes are generally retained for up to <strong>three years after the end of the working relationship</strong>, unless there is a legal or compelling reason to retain particular information for longer.</li>
          <li>Data from enquiries that do not lead to a working relationship are generally deleted within <strong>12 months</strong> when no longer needed.</li>
          <li>Invoices and other records that form part of the tax administration are retained for the period required by Dutch tax law, generally <strong>seven years</strong>.</li>
          <li>Data that are no longer required for their purpose are deleted or anonymised.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>10.7 Data Security</h3>
        <p>
          Appropriate technical and organisational measures are used to protect personal data against loss, misuse, unauthorised access, alteration, or disclosure. Access to Client files is restricted to the Coach, except where a service provider necessarily processes data in providing its service.
        </p>

        <h3>10.8 Your Data Protection Rights</h3>
        <p>
          Depending on the circumstances, individuals may have rights to access, correct, delete, restrict or object to the processing of their personal data, and to data portability. Where processing is based on consent, consent can be withdrawn at any time without affecting the lawfulness of processing before withdrawal. Requests can be sent to <a href="mailto:info@arianemader.com"><u>info@arianemader.com</u></a> and will normally be handled within one month.
        </p>

        <h3>10.9 Complaints About Data Protection</h3>
        <p>
          Individuals have the right to lodge a complaint with the Dutch Data Protection Authority (<strong>Autoriteit Persoonsgegevens</strong>) or, where applicable, another competent supervisory authority.
        </p>

        <h3>10.10 Website Analytics</h3>
        <p>
          This website uses <strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong> to obtain privacy-focused, aggregated information about website use. Cloudflare Web Analytics does not use cookies or local storage for analytics and is not used by Ariane Mader to identify individual visitors or for advertising or marketing. The website is hosted using <strong>GitHub Pages</strong>.
        </p>
        <div class="my-12 border-t border-gray-300"></div>

          <h2 class="blueFont">11. Changes to These Terms and Privacy Policy</h2>
          <p>
            These Terms and the Privacy Policy may be updated when legal requirements, professional standards, services, or data-processing practices change. The version applicable to an existing agreement will not be changed retroactively to the Client’s disadvantage without a valid legal basis or agreement. The current version will be published on this website.
          </p>
        </div>
    </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


</BaseLayout>
